💡 INTERPRETATION:
- Analysis uses only the FIRST 7 DIMENSIONS of each action vector (first action)
- All correlations are computed per-dimension (each action component independently)
- Mean Correlation = average of per-dimension correlations across all 7 dimensions
- Within-dataset results show how similar different layers are within the correct task
- Cross-dataset results show how wrong task layers compare to the correct task layer 12
- Lower correlations in cross-dataset results suggest task-specific representations
- Higher MSE in cross-dataset results indicates greater differences between tasks
- Max/Min correlations identify which specific action dimensions are most/least preserved
